> We are trying to represent 454 pyrosequcing plates.  Here we use
> geom_bin2d to visualize the number of reads across the plate.
>
> sample:
> http://bioinfo-mite.ibest.uidaho.edu/projects/454QaReport/raw-attachment/wiki/WikiStart/sidebyside.pdf
>
> We want to create this exact graph, but qual as the fill, so we can
> directly compare number of reads in each regions vs quality in the
> same region.

In that case, you'll need to do something like:

all.data <- transform(all.data,
  binx = round_any(x, 10),
  biny = round_any(y, 10)
)
sum.data <- ddply(all.data, c("binx", "biny"), summarise,
  n = length(binx),  qual = mean(qual), .progress = "text")

And then plot the results of sum.data with bin2d.

Hadley

